# Every stage directory is a Docker build context and every stage Dockerfile
# copies the whole of it into the image, so anything left lying about here gets
# baked in.  Nothing below is a file the stage needs: it is the debris that
# accumulates from running the suite locally, plus editor backups.  The same
# list ships in all three of this task's stage directories -- a stage that
# excluded something the others kept would produce an image nobody could
# reproduce from the tree.
#
# Every pattern is `**/`-prefixed, which is not decoration.  These are not
# gitignore patterns: Docker anchors an unprefixed pattern at the context root
# and its `*` does not cross a `/`, so a bare `__pycache__/` guards this
# directory and nothing beneath it.  Measured rather than assumed -- with the
# unprefixed list, `docker export` of a `FROM scratch` + `COPY .` image still
# contained lib/__pycache__/catalog.cpython-310.pyc,
# lib/.pytest_cache/CACHEDIR.TAG and data/documents/x.yaml~.  The `**/` form
# matches at the root too, so one pattern per kind covers both depths.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/*~
**/*.orig
**/*.rej
**/.DS_Store
